post.description:
Evaluate web page HTML code against a given *ruleset*. HTML code may be passed either as plain text or ZIP archive.

### Improving the accessibility results

For a more precise evaluation of a web page, UsableNet recommends processing the HTML DOM using a precompiled JavaScript library prepared and maintained by UsableNet.

This library is available at <https://aqa.usablenet.com/aqapool/js/aqa-analyzer.js>.

To process the original HTML DOM:

```javascript
const htmlString = await window._aqaProcessDOM();
```

This returns a processed DOM description that, when passed to `/a11y/tests/evaluate` endpoint, returns more precise results. The script should be injected when `document.body` is available, the function whenever you wish to snapshot the page.

Here's a sample script:

```javascript
async function makeSnapshot() {
    // The analyzer script URL
    const scriptUrl = 'https://aqa.usablenet.com/aqapool/js/aqa-analyzer.js';
    let snapshot = '';

    // Fetch the script and evaluate it to the webpage
    if (window._aqaProcessDOM === undefined) {
        let response = await fetch(scriptUrl);
        response = await response.text();
        window.eval(response);
    }

    // Call the function that will retrieve a snapshot of the page as string
    snapshot = await window._aqaProcessDOM();
    return snapshot;
}
console.log(await makeSnapshot());
```

Alternatively, add the script instead of evaluating it:

```javascript
async function makeSnapshot() {
    // The analyzer script URL
    const scriptUrl = 'https://aqa.usablenet.com/aqapool/js/aqa-analyzer.js';
    let snapshot = '';

    // Add the script to document.head if missing
    if (window._aqaProcessDOM === undefined) {
        await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
            const script = document.createElement('script');
            script.onload = () => {
                resolve();
            }
            script.onerror = () => {
                reject('Failed to load aqa-analyzer script');
            }
            script.src = scriptUrl;
            document.head.appendChild(script);
        });
    }

    // Call the function that will retrieve a snapshot of the page as string
    snapshot = await window._aqaProcessDOM();
    return snapshot;
}
console.log(await makeSnapshot());
```
